  "question": "What do the Vimose runes say?",
  "answer": "The Vimose inscriptions comprise several short texts, including \"harja,\" \"aadagasu / laasauwija,\" \"mariha [.]ala / makija,\" \"talijo gisai oj / tkbis hleuno an[.] regu,\" \"awgns,\" and \"[w]agni[ŋ]o\" [S3]. According to the published translation summarized on Wikipedia, \"harja\" is \"likely a personal name or 'comb'/'warrior'\" [S3]. The sequence \"mariha ... makija\" is interpreted as \"possibly 'Mari (the famous one) is the sword of Alla'\" [S3], while \"awgns\" is read as \"possibly 'son/descendant of Awa'\" [S3]. The source notes that \"several inscriptions remain only partially deciphered\" [S3], so not all of the Vimose texts have an agreed meaning.",
